# Drought: "Activated abilities cost an additional "Sacrifice a Swamp" to activate for each black mana symbol in their
# activation costs." (CR 118.8, 602.2b), and "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice this enchantment unless you pay
# {W}{W}." Bot2 casts the blue Drowned with its Swamp out and keeps the Swamp (a spell with no black symbol), then activates
# Drowned's "{B}: Regenerate" with the Swamp's own mana and sacrifices it; with no Swamp left that ability is refused, though
# an untapped Mox Jet could pay its {B}.
# Bot1's Fetid Heath "{W/B}, {T}: Add ..." is a mana ability whose hybrid {W/B} is a black mana symbol (the ruling, CR
# 107.4e): refused on turn 3 with no Swamp, it takes the Swamp on turn 5. Bot1 pays the upkeep {W}{W} exactly on turns 3
# and 5 and declines on turn 7: Drought is sacrificed, and the Heath's ability then costs no Swamp.
